# Triaged gitleaks findings, suppressed by FINGERPRINT only.
#
# A fingerprint is commit:file:rule:line, so each entry silences exactly one
# match at one line of one commit. Never suppress by path or by rule here, and
# never widen an allowlist in .gitleaks.toml to make a finding go away: that
# would blind the scan to everything else at that path.
#
# These two were found by the first scan that actually covered every ref
# (gitleaks 8.30.1, --log-opts=--all). The previous action-based job scanned a
# commit range and reported "0 commits scanned" on merge pushes, so it had never
# looked at either line.
#
